@6. The traps, collected
.
=6. THE TRAPS, COLLECTED
.
.Every one of these has cost a debugging session at least once.
.
.  P AND 255 on a heap or VRAM address
.      WHAT HAPPENS: AND is 16-bit signed; above 32767 it raises OUT OF RANGE
.        instead of masking
.      DO THIS: H = INT(P/256) : L = P - H*256
.
.  an address in an A% variable
.      WHAT HAPPENS: % is signed 16-bit and truncates silently -- A% = 49152
.        reads back -16,384
.      DO THIS: untyped variable, or split into page and offset
.
.  $0400 for machine code
.      WHAT HAPPENS: stock BASIC leaves it free, a compiled GPC program does
.        not -- runtime state lives there, and it corrupts silently
.      DO THIS: banked RAM, $A000-$BFFF
.
.  PRINT after GP.PRINTAT
.      WHAT HAPPENS: GP drawing never calls the KERNAL, so the cursor is
.        wherever it was
.      DO THIS: LOCATE first, or stay in one world
.
.  SORT.INC.BL with no #SYMFILE
.      WHAT HAPPENS: {VAR} cannot resolve a crunched name -- NO SYMBOL FILE
.        FOR {}
.      DO THIS: #SYMFILE "@:PROG.SYM", before the #INCLUDEs
.
.  GP.BOX X,Y,W,H,,7
.      WHAT HAPPENS: optionals cannot be skipped over
.      DO THIS: GP.BOX X,Y,W,H,0,7
.
.  SCREEN after BMX.PAINT
.      WHAT HAPPENS: reloads the default palette and throws the image's
.        colours away
.      DO THIS: set the mode first
.
.  STR.FIELD$ wanted bigger
.      WHAT HAPPENS: auto-DIMed at 0..10 on first use, and you cannot DIM it
.        after
.      DO THIS: DIM it before the first call, set STR.MAX
.
.  #DEFINE X 129536
.      WHAT HAPPENS: #DEFINE takes an INT16 -- ERROR: INVALID PARAMETER
.      DO THIS: an ordinary variable
.
.  a GP. keyword in a hand-written .bas
.      WHAT HAPPENS: the ROM cannot LIST or RUN a $CE7x token
.      DO THIS: expected -- compile it
.
.  readable names in a hand-written .bas
.      WHAT HAPPENS: the built-in BASIC gives TWO significant characters --
.        THEME.CLR and THEME.COUNT become one variable, silently
.      DO THIS: write BASL, or give every variable a distinct first two
.        characters
.
.The last one is worth its own sentence. Inside BASL you are safe -- 64
.significant characters, so PANEL.COL and PANEL.ROW are genuinely different
.variables and the readable names cost nothing. Write the same test as a raw
..bas for the host tokeniser and the two-character rule is back. It cost two
.test cycles during tier 6, both times looking exactly like a compiler bug.
.
.Dotted names also dodge the keyword-collision trap: MENUVERT.COUNT,
.THEME.CLR, LINEINPUT.LEN and LINEINPUT.RETURN all contain reserved words and
.all work, because BASLOAD matches the whole identifier. An undotted one does
.not -- POS, MB, ST, LEN, CHAR cannot be variables at all. That is the main
.reason the library is dotted throughout.
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>37|4.7 SORT.INC.BL -- shell sort a string array
